			<div class="content" id="post-content-1927543">
									

<p>Neutral vote for now.</p>
<p>This is a little&#8230; confusing right now. It's not that I don't understand what's going on, I'm pretty sure I do, though you hint that this is derived from a legend and you also hint at something deeper and more sinister in the [REDACTED] portions, and I've no idea what either could be.</p>
<p>Maybe I'm woozy from my new diet, but other people seem to feel the same way. I guess what I'm saying is that it's difficult to read, and there's not enough payout for it. I don't mind a difficult, overly technical read if the payout is big or if its something I'm really interested in. But this is neither for me, right now. I feel like the containment procedures could be shortened to like three sentences and still make sense, and that a lot of the description could be ironed out. Maybe you should simplify it out, or maybe make the hook a little more obvious, or maybe both.</p>
<p>This is only a gut feeling, so don't take it as gospel. Whenever I see a confusing article, I usual come back and re-read it after having a day or so to think about it. I'll vote + or - then.</p>

