			<div class="content" id="post-content-1927557">
									

<p>This is a solid attempt, but in the end I can't get behind this one. Part of it is that there's a lot of things on the periphery that I feel are distracting. Like the future-predicting satellite that's necessary for containment, or the Horizon Initiative being involved. There's too many moving parts, in my opinion, for the narrative that you're going for. On top of that, you've got an interpretation of the Foundation that seems to involve it being many centuries old, which is interesting to me, but when it's thrown in with all the other stuff on the side you've got going, it feels like yet another distraction.</p>
<p>Conceptually, I find the idea of duelling sets of astral projections fighting and affecting that year's agricultural outlook interesting, but I feel that it loses something in the translation. Like, as a folk legend, I find it really intriguing, and I think it would be really cool to hang out at a tavern somewhere and listen to some old Italian farmer's tales of spiritual battles with crazy famine-imps from his youth. As a scientific report of anomalous phenomena, it's just not working for me.</p>
<p>There's a few wording errors related to the finer points of the English language still in the article; I'll take a look in a minute and fix up a few things, but you may want to read this over once more and check for small errors.</p>
<p>One last thing:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Soldatesca Cavalleria of Pisa</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I really, really wish people would stop doing this.</p>

